## Problem

After `registerDraggable()` calls `gameObject.setInteractive({ draggable: true })` and `scene.input.setDraggable(gameObject, true)`, the sprite is added to Phaser's `_pendingInsertion` queue but not yet to the active hit-test list (`_list`). A pointer click arriving before the next `preUpdate` flush is silently ignored.

## Root Cause

Phaser's InputPlugin only processes `_pendingInsertion` during `PRE_UPDATE` system events. At 60fps, the window is ~16ms. During the deal animation, `onDealComplete()` → `makeDraggable()` → `registerDraggable()` fires, and a player's first click may land in this narrow window.

## Fix

In `src/ui/dragDrop.ts`, `registerDraggable()`, after `setInteractive` and `setDraggable`, directly flush `_pendingInsertion` into `_list`:

```ts
const input = scene.input as any;
if (input._pendingInsertion && input._list) {
  for (let i = 0; i < input._pendingInsertion.length; i++) {
    const obj = input._pendingInsertion[i];
    if (!input._list.includes(obj)) {
      input._list.push(obj);
    }
  }
  input._pendingInsertion.length = 0;
}
```

This is additive, backward-compatible, and does not alter existing drag semantics. It ensures the object is hit-testable immediately after registration.

## Acceptance Criteria

1. After `registerDraggable()` is called, the registered object is immediately in the hit-test list.
2. The fix applies to all consumers of `DragDropManager` (Main Street, Golf, Coloretto, Gym, BC) — run their existing browser suites to verify no regression.

## Key Files

- `src/ui/dragDrop.ts` — `registerDraggable()` method

